<title>UK: Not clear stability pact agreed in Dublin - Clarke.</title>
<headline>Not clear stability pact agreed in Dublin - Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said it was highly unlikely that a stability pact for countries in a single European currency would be decided at next Monday's meeting of finance ministers and not clear that it would be settled at the December 13/14 Dublin EU summit.</p>
<p>&quot;It will not be concluded next Monday, it was highly unlikely ever to be concluded next Monday,&quot; he told Parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not even sure it will be concluded at Dublin.&quot;</p>
<p>Clarke said he would enter a &quot;parliamentary reserve&quot; on any decisions until the House of Commons was satisfied that its scrutiny process had been completed.</p>
